## 4. Comparison matrix

| Type | Force density | Distal mass | Vacuum | Leak risk | Backdrive / safety | Bandwidth | EcoSuit role |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| In-joint geared electric | Med | High | OK with dry/vac lube | None | Poor unless clutched | High | Elbow/knee only if clutched |
| Rotary SEA | Med | Med | OK | None | Good | Med-high | Hip + knee primary |
| QDD | Med-low | Med-high | OK | None | Excellent | High | Ankle / later hip |
| Cable / Bowden | Med | Low at joint | OK; dust is the enemy | None | Good with spring | Med | Shoulder, elbow, glove, ankle |
| Cable-SEA | Med | Low at joint | OK; dust | None | Good | Med | Preferred remote drive |
| Open hydraulics | Very high | High system | Hard | High | Design-dependent | High | Reject |
| EHA (self-contained) | High | Med | Possible | Medium | Design-dependent | High | Only if electric cannot hit torque |
| PAM / pneumatics | Med in muscle | Low at joint | Compressor/heat problem | Medium (closed loop) | Intrinsic compliance | Low-med | Glove / maybe elbow |
| Springs + clutches | Low | Very low | Excellent | None | Excellent (opens on loss) | n/a | Layer 0 on every joint |
| SMA | High local | Very low | Heat problem | None | Poor / slow | Low | Glove, latches |
| Vacuum-gap electrostatic | High W/kg, low absolute force | Very low | Native advantage | None | TBD | High | Latches, visor, wrist coupons |

