## 5. Joint-by-joint downselect

| Joint | Job | Do not use | MK.I pick | Why |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Hip flex/ext | Walk, kneel, stand from squat | SMA, PAM as primary | Rotary SEA or EHA LRU on the pelvic yoke | Highest torque, needs compliance |
| Hip abd/rot | Sidestep, turn | Powered (at first) | Passive bearings + soft stop | X1 lesson |
| Knee | Walk, kneel, stairs | Hydraulic plant | Rotary SEA in the thigh longeron, or cable-SEA from the yoke | High cycle, must backdrive |
| Ankle | Push-off, balance | Big gearbox | QDD or cable-SEA; spring-clutch for MK.I | Powered ankle on X1 improved push-off and balance |
| Waist | Bend to pick up | Full servo | Passive convolute + optional lock | Hard-suit already gives you the bearing |
| Shoulder flex | Reach, tools | In-joint harmonic | Cable-SEA from dorsal pack or small SEA behind pauldron | Volume under plates is the limit |
| Elbow | Tools, hold | Hydraulic | Cable from upper-arm or small SEA | Moderate torque, high cycle |
| Wrist / glove | Fatigue, grip | Anything bulky | SMA or PAM or tendon glove exo | Already a researched EVA problem |
| Plate latches / visor | Open armor, don | Walk-class motors | Vacuum-gap electrostatic or SMA | Tiny, vacuum-native |

