## 6. Recommended MK.I hybrid

**Layer 0 — passive**
- Gravity-balance springs at the shoulder
- Suit-torque-cancel springs at elbow and knee
- Mechanical clutches that open on power loss

**Layer 1 — work joints**
- Rotary SEAs at hip flex and knee
- Packaged in the pelvic yoke and thigh longeron so plates can come off over them

**Layer 2 — remote electric**
- Bowden or tendon SEAs for elbow, ankle, and shoulder
- Motors in the dorsal lattice next to the PLSS where you can cool and swap them

**Layer 3 — glove**
- Separate tendon or SMA/PAM package
- Do not wait for the gait system

**Not in MK.I**
- Ship-wide hydraulics
- Suit-gas pneumatics
- SMA on the legs
- Electrostatic as a walk actuator

Power architecture: one bus on the PLSS. Actuators are LRUs. Default state on power loss is free or clutched-open, never locked, except for a voluntary parking brake the crew sets.

Thermal: every watt the motor does not turn into torque becomes a problem against a ceramic-hemp stack designed as an insulator. Prefer efficiency and remote motors over more torque in the joint.

Control: impedance first, position almost never.

This stack matches how X1 was built, how EVA glove research actually looks, and how the EcoSuit plates want to be serviced. It keeps the Iron Man read (visible joint pods, armor that opens) without pretending a harmonic drive belongs inside every segment.

---

## 7. Failure modes to design against

| Failure | Outcome if ignored | Mitigation |
|---|---|---|
| Seized gearbox | Locked joint, cannot walk or don | Clutch / freewheel path; no unclutched harmonic as sole path |
| Cut / jammed cable | Lost DOF | Antagonist pair; inspectable sheath; dust boots |
| Hydraulic leak | Contamination, slip, toxicity review | Do not use open hydraulics inside the garment |
| PAM / pneumatic leak | Assist loss; possible pressure interaction | Closed loop only; never suit O2 |
| Motor overheat under plates | Bond lift on hemp-ceramic stack | Remote motors; thermal isolators; current limits |
| Power loss | Suit becomes dead weight or a cage | Passive springs still work; joints free |
| Software runaway | Suit fights the crew | Hard torque / velocity caps in firmware and analog cutoff |

